 "notes": "Kingdon trap: a charged inner rod (-2300 V) on the axis of a grounded can, r-z symmetric. The radial field is logarithmic - no radial minimum - so nothing is trapped by the field alone: ions are held by ANGULAR MOMENTUM, orbiting the rod (launch direction has a tangential component). Compact geometry: the earlier example scaled by 0.65 radially and 0.76 axially (rod r 5.2 mm, can inner r 13.0 mm, length 82.0 mm; the r-scaling preserves ln(b/a), so the original voltage and launch energy still balance). Orbits verified: r stays within 8.4-10.1 mm for the full 400 us flight.",
